a","Tribulato, 2012, Siculi bilingues? Latin in the inscriptions of early Roman Sicily","Ampolo, Erdas, 2019, Inscriptiones Segestanae. Le iscrizioni greche e latine di Segesta",[265,265,266,267,268,269,270,271,272],"R46KDTZX","77P5MNIR","WHBJDH75","U7GGTWQM","4FSSHE62","Z54HF9PD","X5ZZ4GPT","3PK3JKXR",[274,275,276,27,32,36,277,277,278,279,277,280,281,138],"isic002737","honorific for lucius iulius agrippa, euergetes",{"_":5},"segesta","sicilia","sicily","parco archeologico di segesta","latin",[],{"title":284,"body":285,"divs":286,"editions":311,"images":321,"handnote":322},"ISic002737. Honorific for Lucius Iulius Agrippa, euergetes","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"la\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>L(ucio) · Iulio · C(aii) · f(ilio) · Agrippae \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>euergetae · \u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>hic · plateam · a · Sosi\u003Cspan class=\"small\" title=\"small character: a\">a\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>usque · ad · fanum · \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>L·IULIO·C·F·AGRIPPAE\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>EUERGETAE·\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>HIC·PLATEAM·A·SOSI\u003Cspan class=\"small\" title=\"small character: a\">A\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>USQUE·AD·FANUM·\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text of I.Segesta, with the addition of interpunctuation on the basis of photograph\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>To Lucius Iulius Agrippa, son of Gaius, euergetes. This man (was responsible for) the street from Sosia all the way to the temple\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The stone is presumably a plaque to be affixed to a statue base, with the word 'hic' referring to the statue of the honorand. Euergetes is the first instance of this Greek word as a calque in Latin. 'a Sosia' presumably refers to a location within the city, and has been suggested to refer to a statue (Dubois), or perhaps a platea or via.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Nenci 1995 1184 no.11 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001415\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001415\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1997 740 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Michelini 1997 n.12 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001746\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001746\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Nenci 1997 1193 tav.CCXXXV.2 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001729\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001729\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1998 608 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001282\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001282\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> 2000 640 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Paci 2008 333-334 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001687\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001687\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Tribulato 2012 314 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001557\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001557\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003Cli> Ampolo and Erdas 2019 L8 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001036\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001036\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>Slightly irregular letters iwth a broad square module, but narrower towards the end of each line. E has upward curling serifs; triangular interpuncts; final A of line 3 is small, at 29mm.\u003C/p> Line 1-4  52-61  Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[287,290,293,296,299,302,305,308],{"id":288,"html":289},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"la\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>L(ucio) · Iulio · C(aii) · f(ilio) · Agrippae \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>euergetae · \u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>hic · plateam · a · Sosi\u003Cspan class=\"small\" title=\"small character: a\">a\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>usque · ad · fanum · \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag; edition source: \u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\">https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3PK3JKXR\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"la\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>L·IULIO·C·F·AGRIPPAE\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>EUERGETAE·\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>HIC·PLATEAM·A·SOSI\u003Cspan class=\"small\" title=\"small character: a\">A\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>USQUE·AD·FANUM·\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":291,"html":292},"facsimile-images","\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>",{"id":294,"html":295},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text of I.Segesta, with the addition of interpunctuation on the basis of photograph\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":297,"html":298},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class